INSERT INTO evidence (code, title, description, type, classification, content, metadata)
VALUES ($nxs$EVID-P30$nxs$, $nxs$Voicemail, Bureau line 4, 29 September 2026$nxs$, $nxs$A 41-second voicemail left on the Bureau’s retention line from a withheld number.$nxs$, $nxs$AUDIO$nxs$::evidence_type, $nxs$RESTRICTED$nxs$::evidence_classification, $nxj${"text":"Voicemail, Bureau line 4, received 29 SEP 2026 02:14, 41 seconds, caller ID withheld, external. A woman’s voice speaks to the Bureau’s retention desk about a record closed two years earlier and asks the Bureau to convene new keepers. The full transcript is attached to the audio record.","state":"UNREVIEWED","artifact_type":"AUDIO","source":"Spire control console","custodian":"Bureau of Continuity Records","provenance":"Original record; first-hand","date":"2026-09-29","captured_at":"2026-09-29","condition":"NORMAL","audio_url":"/audio/case/44f20058a2d4a8.mp3","transcript":"[line hiss] [voicemail beep] VEY: This is for the Bureau, the retention desk. You will know the voice. A record you hold was closed two years ago. One check on it was left empty, on purpose. It was never mine to fill. I held none of it. That is the design. The three who closed it cannot judge themselves. I am asking for a second quorum: three who were not there. Do not look for me. [handset click]","relationships":[{"to":"EVID-P28","kind":"CORROBORATES","note":"Same voice as the answering speaker in fragment 5."},{"to":"EVID-P29","kind":"EXPLAINS","note":"The message asks for new keepers because the rule needs three who are not interested parties."}]}$nxj$::jsonb, $nxj${"node":"P30","reliability":"primary","custodian":"Bureau of Continuity Records","source":"Spire control console"}$nxj$::jsonb)
